WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.000 --> 00:01.000
MkvDrama.net

3
00:00.000 --> 00:06.024
[Closing Notice]

4
00:33.050 --> 00:34.510
Nakarai.

5
00:41.740 --> 00:45.620
It all started with an email sent by mistake.

6
00:51.460 --> 00:53.585
[No Subject] Did you receive an email

7
00:53.585 --> 00:55.820
from Gourmet Map today?

8
00:55.820 --> 00:59.300
I meant to send it to myself, but it went to you by mistake.

9
00:59.300 --> 01:03.410
I'm sorry. I just wanted to apologize.

10
01:03.410 --> 01:07.780
I've been living with my girlfriend for two years.

11
01:07.780 --> 01:12.530
But there's one thing that's been bothering me,

12
01:12.530 --> 01:14.320
and that is...

13
01:14.320 --> 01:18.530
I'm living with my best friend from my school days.

14
01:18.530 --> 01:24.160
Of course, he's a guy, but I've fallen for him.

15
01:24.160 --> 01:28.190
Now I want to have sex with him and have him hold me.

16
01:32.580 --> 01:34.210
What are you doing?

17
01:37.750 --> 01:39.650
I'm with the person I like.

18
01:39.650 --> 01:43.560
We live together, and we'll probably get married.

19
01:43.560 --> 01:48.730
It's weighing on my mind, but I wonder if it's that big of a deal.

20
01:48.730 --> 01:53.040
I think you're kind for trying to endure it alone.

21
01:53.040 --> 01:55.080
Because you like her,

22
01:55.080 --> 01:59.190
you don't want to trouble her or clash with her.

23
01:59.190 --> 02:01.313
The person I'd been emailing openly with,

24
02:01.313 --> 02:04.340
thinking we were complete strangers,

25
02:04.340 --> 02:06.380
was my coworker.

26
02:06.380 --> 02:08.600
I think I'm being kind

27
02:09.350 --> 02:12.030
because I want her to do it with me.

28
02:13.570 --> 02:15.720
All I have

29
02:15.720 --> 02:18.570
are dirty ulterior motives inside.

30
02:19.160 --> 02:21.000
It sickens me.

31
02:21.000 --> 02:22.700
Maybe next time.

32
02:24.394 --> 02:26.114
It's late.

33
02:36.166 --> 02:37.886
Are you awake?

34
02:38.586 --> 02:41.316
I don't know how to say this,

35
02:41.316 --> 02:43.756
but I just want a reply.

36
02:43.756 --> 02:47.906
I want to have sex with you, Nakarai.

37
02:49.196 --> 02:50.646
Yeah.

38
02:52.066 --> 02:53.476
Okay.

39
02:53.476 --> 02:55.486
When it rains, it pours.

40
02:55.486 --> 02:59.086
Doesn't that kind of sound like us?

41
02:59.086 --> 03:01.856
You don't need this body...

42
03:01.856 --> 03:04.616
Saying that now is unfair.

43
03:06.246 --> 03:08.316
It almost made me cry.

44
03:10.216 --> 03:13.796
Well, it's the truth.

45
03:17.266 --> 03:22.226
Hagiwara, you're neither bad nor dirty.

46
03:22.226 --> 03:26.566
It's something I've always lacked and always wanted.

47
03:26.566 --> 03:30.936
Something I desperately sought, as if begging for rain.

48
03:30.936 --> 03:34.236
Say it. You go first, Kazuaki.

49
03:34.236 --> 03:35.786
Say it.

50
03:43.876 --> 03:45.996
I've found someone I like.

51
03:49.166 --> 03:50.966
Let's break up.

52
03:56.926 --> 03:58.346
Goodbye.

53
03:59.746 --> 04:01.836
Baby steps are fine.

54
04:04.626 --> 04:09.026
I'll take baby steps too

55
04:10.375 --> 04:12.775
and walk on my own.

56
04:13.586 --> 04:16.246
What do you mean you might disappear?

57
04:18.746 --> 04:21.226
I'm not going anywhere.

58
04:21.226 --> 04:24.166
It's a long story, though.

59
04:26.206 --> 04:27.816
Then never mind.

60
04:27.816 --> 04:29.306
You're kidding.

61
04:35.736 --> 04:37.506
I like you, Hagiwara.

62
04:40.386 --> 04:42.006
I want to be with you.

63
04:46.296 --> 04:48.046
Me too.

64
04:48.046 --> 04:51.576
It was always raining.

65
04:51.576 --> 04:55.286
We were always in the rain.

66
05:46.326 --> 05:48.856
Well, Hagiwara, welcome back.

67
05:48.856 --> 05:50.946
- Thanks. - Welcome back.

68
05:50.946 --> 05:52.506
Cheers.

69
05:56.106 --> 05:57.506
That's tasty.

70
06:00.966 --> 06:04.746
Did you eat herring roe kimchi in Osaka?

71
06:04.746 --> 06:07.796
No, since I couldn't go buy any.

72
06:07.796 --> 06:11.116
What? But I even emailed you about it.

73
06:11.116 --> 06:14.856
It looked super good when I saw it on TV.

74
06:16.056 --> 06:17.666
Lucky.

75
06:17.666 --> 06:20.496
I like that it's not a trip, but a temporary position.

76
06:20.496 --> 06:22.836
You get to live there for a while.

77
06:22.836 --> 06:24.686
That's what I thought too.

78
06:24.686 --> 06:27.406
But my tourism energy didn't last long.

79
06:27.406 --> 06:30.186
In the end, I'd sleep on my days off.

80
06:32.376 --> 06:33.856
Excuse me.

81
06:33.856 --> 06:35.836
Salted tongue and galbi.

82
06:38.726 --> 06:41.586
Thank you. Enjoy your meal.

83
06:42.266 --> 06:43.516
No, you can't.

84
06:43.516 --> 06:46.226
I told you, the tongue goes first.

85
06:57.466 --> 07:00.396
You haven't changed, Hagiwara.

86
07:00.396 --> 07:03.446
A four-month absence isn't gonna change me.

87
07:09.876 --> 07:13.696
By the way, did your room get any better?

88
07:13.696 --> 07:15.556
Same as always.

89
07:15.556 --> 07:17.336
What do you mean?

90
07:17.336 --> 07:20.296
Oh, you still haven't been to this guy's place, have you?

91
07:20.296 --> 07:23.506
- No. - It's a run-down 40-year-old apartment.

92
07:23.506 --> 07:24.586
37.

93
07:24.586 --> 07:26.466
Same difference.

94
07:26.466 --> 07:30.236
Apparently, because it's old, he can do whatever he wants to it.

95
07:30.236 --> 07:33.026
He started making shelves and never finished.

96
07:33.026 --> 07:34.526
Why shelves?

97
07:36.446 --> 07:39.366
Just felt like it suddenly.

98
07:42.366 --> 07:45.056
Hagiwara, could you help him out?

99
07:45.056 --> 07:46.186
You can charge him.

100
07:46.186 --> 07:47.486
Don't say that.

101
07:47.486 --> 07:49.786
Something has to be done.

102
07:49.786 --> 07:52.746
A messy home means a messy heart.

103
07:53.736 --> 07:54.756
Sure.

104
07:54.756 --> 07:56.736
I'll help if that's okay.

105
07:56.736 --> 07:58.426
Not a pro, though.

106
08:02.066 --> 08:04.616
See? That's great.

107
08:04.616 --> 08:07.176
- Dig in. - Thanks.

108
08:22.056 --> 08:25.974
[No Subject - New Co-op] [Mizunomori 102 Arakawa-ku, Tokyo]

109
08:28.516 --> 08:30.166
It's so hot.

110
08:41.016 --> 08:44.821
[Large Watermelon] [On Sale]

111
08:54.616 --> 08:58.266
He did say he wanted to be with me, but...

112
09:02.336 --> 09:04.716
we both ended up empty-handed.

113
09:04.716 --> 09:09.436
It wasn't as smooth as an "Okay, let's start dating" development.

114
09:16.306 --> 09:18.166
What are you carrying?

115
09:23.396 --> 09:25.006
A watermelon.

116
09:25.774 --> 09:27.324
Why?

117
09:29.946 --> 09:31.516
Why, indeed?

118
09:32.866 --> 09:34.556
Seriously?

119
09:50.116 --> 09:51.616
Look at this.

120
09:55.256 --> 09:57.286
Did kids measure their heights here?

121
09:57.286 --> 09:58.536
Probably.

122
09:59.126 --> 10:03.866
There are nail holes and sticker marks everywhere.

123
10:03.866 --> 10:07.666
But I liked it as soon as I saw it, so I moved in.

124
10:07.666 --> 10:11.506
There are no tall buildings around, so the sky looks huge.

125
10:13.620 --> 10:15.300
Want a drink?

126
10:15.300 --> 10:18.210
I have barley tea, iced coffee, or beer.

127
10:18.210 --> 10:19.410
Barley tea.

128
10:19.410 --> 10:20.980
So?

129
10:21.700 --> 10:24.070
What else besides the sky?

130
10:28.460 --> 10:33.510
I liked how far the station is, because I wanted a nice walk home.

131
10:35.670 --> 10:37.160
I see.

132
10:40.040 --> 10:41.470
Here.

133
10:41.470 --> 10:42.830
Thanks.

134
10:46.680 --> 10:50.560
Hey, Hagiwara, do you like watermelons that much?

135
10:50.560 --> 10:53.570
Not really. I haven't eaten one this year.

136
10:53.570 --> 10:56.080
So you don't like it?

137
10:56.080 --> 10:59.020
What are we going to do with this giant thing?

138
10:59.020 --> 11:01.160
It won't fit in the fridge.

139
11:01.160 --> 11:03.370
Sorry, I'll take it home.

140
11:03.370 --> 11:05.096
You serious?

141
11:05.096 --> 11:06.780
It's in the way, right?

142
11:07.480 --> 11:11.450
If there's nowhere to put it, we just have to go buy one.

143
11:13.172 --> 11:15.830
- A fridge? - Of course not.

144
11:23.190 --> 11:25.000
This is nice.

145
11:25.000 --> 11:27.480
It belongs in a comedy skit.

146
11:27.480 --> 11:29.270
It has character.

147
11:29.270 --> 11:31.310
What kind of character?

148
11:31.310 --> 11:33.670
Is this useful, besides for watermelons?

149
11:33.670 --> 11:36.030
- It's useful. - How?

150
11:36.030 --> 11:38.380
The water heater might suddenly break,

151
11:38.380 --> 11:41.140
so I might wash up on the balcony.

152
11:41.140 --> 11:44.370
Or I might wash laundry by hand if the machine breaks.

153
11:44.370 --> 11:45.790
That's a stretch.

154
11:45.790 --> 11:47.280
It's fine.

155
11:49.450 --> 11:52.940
We need it right now. That's all that matters.

156
11:52.940 --> 11:55.910
I don't care how I use it after today.

157
11:56.500 --> 11:58.480
Great mindset.

158
11:58.480 --> 11:59.830
You think so?

159
12:03.930 --> 12:05.290
Rain?

160
12:05.960 --> 12:07.660
Let's run home.

161
12:07.660 --> 12:10.550
We found a use for it right away.

162
12:18.190 --> 12:19.730
It's so loud!

163
12:19.730 --> 12:21.060
This is crazy.

164
12:21.060 --> 12:23.150
I can't hear a thing!

165
12:26.960 --> 12:28.690
I'll carry it.

166
12:49.960 --> 12:51.240
I like you.

167
12:54.358 --> 12:55.738
I can't hear you.

168
12:56.600 --> 12:59.620
Huh? Oh...

169
12:59.620 --> 13:00.930
I said...

170
13:04.590 --> 13:06.980
You heard me, didn't you?

171
13:06.980 --> 13:08.630
I didn't.

172
13:09.660 --> 13:12.050
I just read your lips.

173
13:13.180 --> 13:14.550
Jeez.

174
13:18.215 --> 13:20.831
You said you wouldn't go anywhere.

175
13:22.790 --> 13:24.120
Sorry.

176
13:25.660 --> 13:28.590
I thought you were over it.

177
13:29.460 --> 13:30.670
Huh?

178
13:31.478 --> 13:34.510
After some time apart,

179
13:34.510 --> 13:38.630
I thought you might've been done with me.

180
13:39.945 --> 13:41.565
Of course not.

181
14:11.490 --> 14:15.010
Do you know how many times I jerked off to you since then?

182
14:15.760 --> 14:18.090
How would I know?

183
14:18.090 --> 14:22.500
I haven't counted either, but a lot.

184
14:22.500 --> 14:24.390
What the hell?

185
14:34.930 --> 14:39.380
I remember the dirty stuff too, but the next morning was the best.

186
14:39.380 --> 14:41.230
You smiled for me.

187
14:42.530 --> 14:44.200
Did I?

188
14:44.800 --> 14:49.140
That face was so beautiful and cute.

189
14:49.140 --> 14:52.970
It made me so happy.

190
14:55.820 --> 14:58.010
Don't say any more.

191
14:58.010 --> 14:59.600
Why?

192
14:59.600 --> 15:03.680
When you say things like that, it raises the bar.

193
15:09.250 --> 15:13.850
After this is over, what face am I supposed to make?

194
15:20.260 --> 15:23.400
Don't think about what happens when it's over.

195
15:23.400 --> 15:25.160
We just started.

196
15:44.711 --> 15:46.161
Nakarai.

197
15:46.861 --> 15:48.191
What?

198
15:49.420 --> 15:53.020
I want to hear your response to what I said earlier.

199
15:55.670 --> 15:57.280
Right now?

200
15:58.041 --> 16:00.331
It's hard to reject me now, right?

201
16:08.860 --> 16:10.410
I like you.

202
16:26.106 --> 16:27.666
Hagiwara.

203
16:33.702 --> 16:35.482
If you get bored of me,

204
16:36.549 --> 16:38.969
don't get tired of my body.

205
16:40.410 --> 16:42.130
Not the other way around?

206
16:42.940 --> 16:44.320
Yeah.

207
16:46.006 --> 16:47.646
That's my line.

208
17:03.200 --> 17:05.830
It's not very cold.

209
17:05.830 --> 17:08.010
I had a feeling it wouldn't be.

210
17:09.453 --> 17:11.263
Seeds are such a pain.

211
17:13.780 --> 17:18.330
Come to think of it, I still haven't finished up your shelves.

212
17:18.330 --> 17:20.360
Finally noticed, huh?

213
17:21.290 --> 17:23.110
But I'm hungry.

214
17:23.930 --> 17:27.740
True. Watermelon isn't filling.

215
17:30.680 --> 17:32.370
What are you craving?

216
17:40.730 --> 17:41.890
I know.

217
17:41.890 --> 17:43.170
What?

218
17:43.170 --> 17:44.760
Temaki sushi.

219
17:44.760 --> 17:46.640
I want temaki sushi.

220
17:46.640 --> 17:48.200
At a sushi place?

221
17:48.200 --> 17:49.750
At home.

222
17:49.750 --> 17:55.020
Buy what we want at the market, put rice in a mixing tub, and roll it.

223
17:55.020 --> 17:56.470
Do we have a tub?

224
17:56.470 --> 17:58.160
No.

225
17:58.160 --> 18:01.760
No, so we'll buy one at the shopping arcade.

226
18:01.760 --> 18:03.690
Again?

227
18:22.620 --> 18:24.620
Hey, Hagiwara.

228
18:24.620 --> 18:26.270
What?

229
18:26.270 --> 18:28.790
Something good happened, huh?

230
18:28.790 --> 18:30.880
What? No.

231
18:30.880 --> 18:32.140
No, you're lying.

232
18:32.140 --> 18:34.490
You're giving off that aura.

233
18:35.180 --> 18:36.680
That's scary.

234
18:39.050 --> 18:42.520
Well, even so, I wouldn't tell you.

235
18:44.220 --> 18:45.650
Well, whatever.

236
18:53.300 --> 18:54.980
I'm going home.

237
18:54.980 --> 18:56.260
Good work today.

238
18:56.260 --> 18:57.580
See you.

239
19:43.950 --> 19:45.870
You promised, didn't you?

240
19:47.230 --> 19:49.470
That you wouldn't break anything.

241
19:51.680 --> 19:53.021
I did.

242
19:54.119 --> 19:55.870
I know.

243
20:00.830 --> 20:02.297
But...

244
20:03.599 --> 20:06.050
when I see your face, I can't help it.

245
20:27.240 --> 20:29.650
Are you locked in again?

246
20:29.650 --> 20:31.260
No.

247
20:35.560 --> 20:39.250
I used the tub again yesterday.

248
20:39.250 --> 20:40.980
For temaki sushi?

249
20:40.980 --> 20:43.980
No, chirashi sushi.

250
20:43.980 --> 20:48.260
I bought the base and mixed it with egg and frozen edamame.

251
20:48.260 --> 20:50.100
Sounds tasty.

252
20:50.100 --> 20:51.910
But I made too much.

253
20:51.910 --> 20:55.820
I had it for lunch today, and it'll probably be dinner too.

254
20:58.810 --> 21:00.860
And the watermelon?

255
21:00.860 --> 21:02.520
Still there.

256
21:02.520 --> 21:03.750
And yours?

257
21:03.750 --> 21:04.910
Mine too.

258
21:04.910 --> 21:10.480
Every time I open the fridge, I'm genuinely surprised it's still here.

259
21:10.480 --> 21:12.720
You're the one who bought it.

260
21:26.954 --> 21:30.244
It's been a while since we last met here.

261
21:31.670 --> 21:35.427
After that, even security was exasperated.

262
21:35.427 --> 21:37.590
"Aren't you one of the admins?", they said.

263
21:37.590 --> 21:39.410
I'm not surprised.

264
21:48.210 --> 21:50.070
I'm going home now.

265
21:50.760 --> 21:52.630
You should go...

266
22:02.130 --> 22:03.980
I want to start over.

267
22:05.200 --> 22:06.570
Huh?

268
22:07.220 --> 22:11.290
When we broke up here before,

269
22:12.110 --> 22:16.450
I was so depressed and frustrated...

270
22:18.714 --> 22:21.014
I want new memories to replace it.

271
22:30.260 --> 22:31.810
Don't laugh.

272
22:32.920 --> 22:34.880
I'm not laughing.

273
22:36.481 --> 22:38.101
You are.

274
22:40.300 --> 22:42.140
You don't know that.

275
22:54.583 --> 22:56.563
Let's make new memories.

276
22:59.140 --> 23:00.510
Okay.

277
23:15.740 --> 23:16.850
Whoa.

278
23:16.850 --> 23:18.440
Don't just watch.

279
23:18.440 --> 23:20.220
You're making me do everything.

280
23:20.220 --> 23:22.640
Hey, you broke up with your girlfriend, right?

281
23:22.640 --> 23:25.420
Want me to introduce you to someone next?

282
23:25.420 --> 23:27.130
Your friend is handsome.

283
23:27.130 --> 23:28.540
Do you have a girlfriend?

284
23:28.540 --> 23:29.940
Someone I'm dating?

285
23:29.940 --> 23:31.240
Well, of course I do.

286
23:31.240 --> 23:33.950
Treat me today, okay?

287
23:33.950 --> 23:35.880
Funding for the festival.

288
23:35.880 --> 23:37.360
Sorry, what do you mean?

289
23:37.360 --> 23:39.020
By the way,

290
23:39.610 --> 23:40.836
why a double?

291
23:40.836 --> 23:43.140
- What is? - The bed.

292
23:43.140 --> 23:45.250
- Is that bad? - No, but...

293
23:45.250 --> 23:46.880
Notice anything?

294
23:46.880 --> 23:49.120
Wait a second, how did you come to that conclusion?

295
23:49.120 --> 23:51.560
I wonder why we're so upset.

296
23:51.560 --> 23:52.960
Don't move.

297
23:52.960 --> 23:55.200
There's such a strong honey feel.

298
23:55.200 --> 23:57.520
It might attract ants.

299
23:57.520 --> 24:00.220
I'll get to you before the ants.

300
24:00.220 --> 24:01.220
MkvDrama.net
